    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **44 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the locality derivation in `OwnerMapper` so it prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n\nThe `locality` mapping previously derived the region purely from the city name. I replaced that inline expression with a call to a new `deriveLocality(owner)` default method that:\n\n1. **Prefers the postcode** \u2014 when a 4-digit postcode is present, it looks up the region by range: NSW `2000-2099`, VIC `3000-3099`, QLD `4000-4099`.\n2. **Falls back to the city-to-region table** (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) when the postcode is absent or outside every known range.\n3. Returns `\"UNKNOWN\"` when neither yields a region.\n\nThis keeps the same result for known cities (e.g. Sydney \u2192 NSW) while disambiguating same-named cities via the postcode. It satisfies both the existing `Cp17` checkpoint (city-based fallback, unknown \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) and the new `Cp30` checkpoint (postcode preferred: a VIC-range `3000` postcode on an unknown city now yields `VIC`).",
