    "probe_text": "The endpoint `POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:179`). Here is every validation and side-effect, in the order it actually happens.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. The caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the method is never entered (403).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 the API interface is `@Validated` and the body is `@Valid` (`OwnersApi.java:86`), so JSR-380 constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` run before the body. On violation \u2192 400. Constraints:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 2 space/`'`/`-` separated parts)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `registrationDate` (optional): `@Valid` only (no constraint)\n\n## Inside the method body, in order\n\n3. **Address normalized first**, then **required-field presence check** (`StringUtils.hasText`): `firstName`, `lastName`, the *normalized* `address`, `city`, `telephone`. Any missing ones are collected and thrown together as `InvalidRequestException` \u2192 400. (Note the address is checked *after* normalization, so a whitespace-only address that passed `@Size` is caught here.)\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n5. **Store normalized address** on the owner (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street-type abbreviations expanded: ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n6. **Normalize telephone to E.164** and store it. Strips separators, assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no `+` is present, requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and enforces fixed national length for known country codes (+61 \u2192 9 digits, +1 \u2192 10). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidRequestException` (400).\n7. **Normalize email** and store it: blank \u2192 `null`; otherwise must match the email pattern (else 400) and is stored lower-cased.\n8. **Validate postcode** (only if present): must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Violation \u2192 400. The value itself is stored/returned as given.\n9. **Default registration date** to `LocalDate.now()` if none supplied.\n10. **Roll registration date to a business day** \u2014 Saturday\u2192+2, Sunday\u2192+1 (Monday); weekdays unchanged. This adjusted date feeds every date-derived value below.\n11. **Daily owner limit** \u2014 count existing owners registered on that (adjusted) date; if `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n12. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** = (that same count `> 80`).\n13. **City capacity** \u2014 count existing owners in the city; if `>= 50` \u2192 `CityCapacityException`.\n14. **Household resolution (side-effect: writes other rows)** \u2014 find existing owners sharing last name + address. If any exist **and** `sharesHousehold == true`: compute a stable `householdId` (first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of `lastName|address`, upper-cased), set it on the new owner, and **backfill + `saveOwner(...)` every existing member** that lacks it.\n15. **Duplicate-identity check** \u2014 build the identity key `<telephone>|<email-or-empty>|<householdId-or-empty>`; if any existing owner has an equal key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 409.\n16. **Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n17. **Set `customerCode`** \u2014 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is the per-city count + 1.\n18. **Set `membershipNumber`** \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the registration year).\n19. **Persist the new owner** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n20. **Populate `householdSize`** \u2014 number of owners sharing the `householdId` (1 if none).\n21. **Map to `OwnerDto`**.\n22. **Emit audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and membershipLevel.\n23. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and **return 201 CREATED** with the DTO.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the \"required field\" check in step 3 duplicates constraints already enforced by Bean Validation in step 2, and several steps (11, 13, 15, 17, 18, 20) each call `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and scan the full owner set."
